1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:03,410
In 1925, a man sold the Eiffel Tower.

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,980
He didn't own it.

3
00:00:05,210 --> 00:00:08,430
Paris 1925, the tower is rusting and

4
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:10,260
expensive to keep standing.

5
00:00:10,490 --> 00:00:12,980
Victor Lustig reads that in a newspaper

6
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:14,820
and sees an opportunity.

7
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:17,190
He forges government letterhead and

8
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,430
invites six scrap dealers to a secret

9
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:21,600
meeting at a luxury hotel.

10
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,240
The city, he says, is quietly selling the

11
00:00:24,310 --> 00:00:27,610
tower for scrap, 7,000 tons of iron, and

12
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:28,960
nobody can know.

13
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:31,650
One dealer Andre Poisson pays, Lustig

14
00:00:31,650 --> 00:00:34,490
takes the money and catches the next train

15
00:00:34,490 --> 00:00:35,340
to Vienna.

16
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:37,530
And Poisson never calls the police.

17
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:39,140
He's too embarrassed.

18
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:41,620
So a month later Lustig comes back and

19
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:43,750
tries to sell the tower again.

20
00:00:44,030 --> 00:00:45,560
Would you have fallen for it?

21
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:47,260
Follow for more true stories.
